            <video controls playsinline preload="none" data-poster="assets/intro/funcad-intro.jpg" aria-label="FunCAD introduction video">
              <source src="assets/intro/funcad-intro.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
              <track kind="captions" src="assets/intro/funcad-intro.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" />
            </video>
            <button class="intro-play" type="button"><span><i><svg><use href="#i-play" /></svg></i>Watch the introduction · 3:06</span></button>
          </figure>
          <figure class="figure-card zoomable" data-reveal data-full="assets/img/fig1.webp">
            <img src="assets/img/fig1.webp" width="1616" height="720" decoding="async" alt="Paper Figure 1: a cup-access request becomes functional goals, an agent-built CAD model tested in simulation, and a printed prototype" />
            <span class="zoom-hint"><svg><use href="#i-zoom" /></svg></span>
            <figcaption><b>Figure 1.</b> From a user request to a printed, working prototype.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="stats" data-reveal>
            <div class="stat"><strong>46</strong><span>mechanism families</span></div>
            <div class="stat"><strong>75</strong><span>agent-built assemblies</span></div>
            <div class="stat"><strong>8<span class="arrow">→</span>22</strong><span>Astra tasks solved: simulation tools → full harness</span></div>
            <div class="stat"><strong>36<small>/46</small></strong><span>Grok with retained history, ≤8 attempts</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="problem" class="section tint">
        <div class="wrap">
          <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
            <span class="kicker">01 · The problem</span>
            <h2>Looks right. Doesn’t work.</h2>
            <p class="sub">Plausible assemblies can hide interference that blocks the function.</p>
          </header>
          <figure class="figure-card zoomable" data-reveal data-full="assets/img/fig7.webp">
            <img src="assets/img/fig7.webp" width="1616" height="532" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Paper Figure 7: an Astra bicycle whose steering intersects the frame, and an Astra clock whose hour wheel overlaps the alarm lever" />
            <span class="zoom-hint"><svg><use href="#i-zoom" /></svg></span>
            <figcaption><b>Figure 7.</b> Astra designs produced without harness feedback.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="viewer-pair" data-reveal>
            <div class="viewer-card">
              <div class="failure-viewer" data-failure-model="bicycle" data-model-coarse="assets/failures/bicycle-failure-detail-coarse.glb?v=20261010-2" data-model-src="assets/failures/bicycle-failure-detail.glb?v=20261010-2"><span class="viewer-status">Loading 3D…</span></div>
              <div class="viewer-label"><span>Cargo bicycle · Astra</span><strong>Steering <i>blocked</i></strong></div>
              <span class="viewer-hint"><svg><use href="#i-orbit" /></svg>Drag to orbit</span>
            </div>
            <div class="viewer-card">
              <div class="failure-viewer" data-failure-model="clock" data-view="1.2 1.05 -1.85" data-model-src="assets/failures/clock-failure-detail.glb?v=20261010-2"><span class="viewer-status">Loading 3D…</span></div>
              <div class="viewer-label"><span>Alarm clock · Astra</span><strong>Hour hand <i>blocked</i></strong></div>
              <span class="viewer-hint"><svg><use href="#i-orbit" /></svg>Drag to orbit</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="center-row" data-reveal>
            <a class="pill on-page" href="demo/"><svg><use href="#i-cube" /></svg>Compare full assemblies in the demo<svg><use href="#i-arrow" /></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="harness" class="section band-dark">
        <div class="wrap">
          <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
            <span class="kicker">02 · FunCAD-Harness</span>
            <h2>Test the function, not the look.</h2>
            <p class="sub">Each requirement becomes a physics test bound to the candidate’s own parts.</p>
          </header>
          <figure class="figure-card zoomable" data-reveal data-full="assets/img/fig5.webp">
            <img src="assets/img/fig5.webp" width="1584" height="668" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Paper Figure 5: FunCAD-Harness connects functional requirements, a candidate mechanism, candidate-specific testbeds, and execution feedback, illustrated with a releasable winch" />
            <span class="zoom-hint"><svg><use href="#i-zoom" /></svg></span>
            <figcaption><b>Figure 5.</b> Requirements → candidate-specific tests → diagnostic feedback.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <ol class="loop" data-reveal>
            <li><b>Requirements</b><span>What it must do</span></li>
            <li><b>Construction</b><span>CAD, joints, assumptions</span></li>
            <li><b>Test binding</b><span>Tests fit this candidate</span></li>
            <li><b>Execution</b><span>Rigid-body physics + audits</span></li>
            <li><b>Revision</b><span>Diagnose and repair</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="simulation" class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
          <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
            <span class="kicker">03 · In simulation</span>
            <h2>Every candidate runs its own test.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="sim-grid" id="sim-grid" data-reveal></div>
          <p class="fine">Replays of recorded FunCAD-Harness tests from our experiment archive · original CAD geometry, display colors.</p>

          <div class="subhead" data-reveal>
            <h3>One task, four designs</h3>
            <p>Task 22 · slider-crank push rod · every build passes</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pair-videos variants" data-sync data-reveal>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/sim/task22_grok.mp4" data-poster="assets/sim/task22_grok.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Grok's slider-crank: vertical crank axis, rod over a drum crank, slider on two rails"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Drum crank<span class="wide-only"> · 9 parts · 44 mm</span></b><span class="agent" data-agent="Grok">Grok</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/sim/task22_fable.mp4" data-poster="assets/sim/task22_fable.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Fable's slider-crank: horizontal crank axis, handwheel, square guide"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Handwheel<span class="wide-only"> · 16 parts · 40 mm</span></b><span class="agent" data-agent="Fable">Fable</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/sim/task22_kimi.mp4" data-poster="assets/sim/task22_kimi.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Kimi's slider-crank: horizontal crank axis, pedestal-mounted hand crank"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Pedestal crank<span class="wide-only"> · 8 parts · 36 mm</span></b><span class="agent" data-agent="Kimi">Kimi</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/sim/task22_astra.mp4" data-poster="assets/sim/task22_astra.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Astra's slider-crank: vertical crank axis, crosshead on twin guide shafts"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Twin guide shafts<span class="wide-only"> · 24 parts · 44 mm</span></b><span class="agent" data-agent="Astra">Astra</span></figcaption></figure>
          </div>
          <p class="fine">Same requirements, four passing designs, each replayed from its recorded loaded test on original CAD geometry in display colors. The last two crank turns of every test are scaled to one common loop, so playback is not real time and speeds are not comparable. Captions give part count and stroke under load.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="revision" class="section tint">
        <div class="wrap">
          <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
            <span class="kicker">04 · Revision</span>
            <h2>Fail. Diagnose. Repair.</h2>
            <p class="sub">Physical feedback tells the agent what broke, so the next revision fixes it.</p>
          </header>
          <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Repair examples" data-reveal>
            <button class="tab" role="tab" id="tab-gripper" aria-controls="panel-gripper" aria-selected="true">Gripper <span class="agent" data-agent="Fable">Fable</span></button>
            <button class="tab" role="tab" id="tab-latch" aria-controls="panel-latch" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Door latch <span class="agent" data-agent="Grok">Grok</span></button>
            <button class="tab" role="tab" id="tab-engine" aria-controls="panel-engine" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Engine linkage <span class="agent" data-agent="Grok">Grok</span></button>
          </div>

          <div class="tab-panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-gripper" aria-labelledby="tab-gripper">
            <div class="revision-layout">
              <figure class="figure-card zoomable tall" data-full="assets/img/fig9.webp">
                <img src="assets/img/fig9.webp" width="1616" height="1149" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Paper Figure 9: Fable's design trajectory for the synchronized parallel gripper, from construction to a repaired design that passes repeated grasp-release cycles" />
                <span class="zoom-hint"><svg><use href="#i-zoom" /></svg></span>
                <figcaption><b>Figure 9.</b> Synchronized parallel gripper, revisions r01 → r02.</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="revision-side">
                <div class="pair-videos">
                  <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/sim/gripper_r01.mp4" data-poster="assets/sim/gripper_r01.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Replay of revision r01: the workpiece tips after release"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>r01<span class="wide-only"> · piece tips over</span></b><span class="agent state-fail">Fail</span></figcaption></figure>
                  <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/sim/gripper.mp4" data-poster="assets/sim/gripper.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Replay of revision r02: both loaded grasp-release cycles succeed"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>r02<span class="wide-only"> · grasps twice</span></b><span class="agent state-pass">Pass</span></figcaption></figure>
                </div>
                <ol class="steps">
                  <li data-mark="✕"><span>Second grasp misses · <b>0 N</b> of 10 N</span></li>
                  <li class="fix" data-mark="↻"><span>Wider pads and rest, 35 N input limit</span></li>
                  <li class="pass" data-mark="✓"><span>Second grasp <b>14.4 N</b> · both cycles pass</span></li>
                </ol>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tab-panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-latch" aria-labelledby="tab-latch" hidden>
            <div class="revision-layout">
              <figure class="figure-card zoomable" data-full="assets/img/fig8.webp">
                <img src="assets/img/fig8.webp" width="1616" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Paper Figure 8: Grok repairs re-locking and local interference in a spring-return door latch across revisions r04 to r06" />
                <span class="zoom-hint"><svg><use href="#i-zoom" /></svg></span>
                <figcaption><b>Figure 8.</b> Spring-return door latch, revisions r04 → r06.</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="revision-side">
                <ol class="steps">
                  <li data-mark="✕"><span>Opens, but never re-locks · <b>13/15</b> checks</span></li>
                  <li class="fix" data-mark="↻"><span>Adds a catching shoulder, relieves the faceplate</span></li>
                  <li class="pass" data-mark="✓"><span><b>15/15</b> checks + geometry audit</span></li>
                </ol>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tab-panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-engine" aria-labelledby="tab-engine" hidden>
            <div class="revision-layout">
              <figure class="figure-card zoomable" data-full="assets/img/fig10.webp">
                <img src="assets/img/fig10.webp" width="1616" height="722" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Paper Figure 10: Grok repairs a twin-cylinder linkage by enlarging the flywheel, clearing a new cylinder contact, and verifying repeated piston motion" />
                <span class="zoom-hint"><svg><use href="#i-zoom" /></svg></span>
                <figcaption><b>Figure 10.</b> Twin-cylinder engine linkage, revisions r01 → r02.</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="revision-side">
                <ol class="steps">
                  <li data-mark="✕"><span>Crank reverses under drive · <b>0</b> full cycles</span></li>
                  <li class="fix" data-mark="↻"><span>Larger flywheel, 5 mm cylinder clearance</span></li>
                  <li class="pass" data-mark="✓"><span><b>8/8</b> checks + geometry audit</span></li>
                </ol>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="prototypes" class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
          <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
            <span class="kicker">05 · Real world</span>
            <h2>Printed. Assembled. Working.</h2>
            <p class="sub">3D-printed prototypes of AI-generated designs.</p>
          </header>
          <div class="proto-grid" data-reveal>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/proto/cup.mp4" data-poster="assets/proto/cup.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Printed cup-access machine raising a rear cup"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Cup-access machine</b><span>Open-ended</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/proto/piston.mp4" data-poster="assets/proto/piston.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Printed piston linkage driven by a crank"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Piston</b><span>Task 17</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/proto/counter.mp4" data-poster="assets/proto/counter.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Printed two-digit mechanical counter"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Two-digit counter</b><span>Task 19</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/proto/timer.mp4" data-poster="assets/proto/timer.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Printed ten-second gravity timer"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Gravity timer</b><span>Task 21</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/proto/lock.mp4" data-poster="assets/proto/lock.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Printed three-digit combination lock"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Combination lock</b><span>Task 18</span></figcaption></figure>
            <figure class="media-card"><video data-src="assets/proto/balls.mp4" data-poster="assets/proto/balls.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Printed three-ball dispenser metering balls"></video><figcaption class="media-cap"><b>Ball dispenser</b><span>Task 20</span></figcaption></figure>
          </div>
